<title>USA: Diana president cuts stake to 11.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Diana president cuts stake to 11.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diana Corp President Donald Runge said he cut his stake in the company to the equivalent of 627,622 common shares, or 11.3 percent of the total, from 743,228 shares, or 13.4 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, Runge said he sold 115,606 shares between Feb 6. and 11 at prices ranging from $11.00 to $13.625 a share.</p>
<p>Runge said he sold off about 16 percent of his holdings in the company to diversify his investments.</p>
</text>
